IDEAS, NO CODE
--------------
Hillium Browser takes ideas, not code, from these projects:
- Zen Browser (zen-browser/desktop), MPL-2.0: the sidebar that holds the
  navigation buttons, the address field and the tabs; pinned tabs as a grid
  of icons above the tab list; compact mode, where the sidebar slides in from
  the window's edge; the page shown as a rounded card; the address field
  floating over the page while you type.
- Brave (brave/brave-browser), MPL-2.0: a per-site switch to turn blocking
  off, with the count of blocked requests next to it.
- Firefox (mozilla-firefox/firefox) and Waterfox (BrowserWorks/waterfox),
  mainly MPL-2.0 (see toolkit/content/license.html in each): the settings
  page laid out as sections with a side list, the bookmarks toolbar toggle,
  inline completion in the address bar, asking before closing a window with
  several tabs, and reading bookmarks from places.sqlite.
- ungoogled-chromium (ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium), BSD-3-Clause:
  its --close-confirmation and --popups-to-tabs switches. Hillium Browser
  does the same in its own code, since Electron's Chromium lacks the patches.
- Web by Nuanced (nuance-dev/Web), MIT: a local assistant that reads the
  page, the command palette, tabs on top or on the side, and private pages
  kept away from the assistant.
- retro-404 (gaoryrt), zabdalimov/win98, MrRar/win98theme,
  spitfirex86/FloatingToolbars, moeleak/win98, rtts/win98: no licence, so
  ideas only, for the Windows 98 look.
- chyinan/liquid-glass-music-player: no licence, ideas only.
- Liquid-glass ideas from archisvaze/liquid-glass, ShengzhiWu/liquid-glass,
  u7663394/LGGC-liquid-glass, kevinbism/liquid-glass-effect,
  xenitV1/liquid-glass-skill, kayozxo/ulauncher-liquid-glass and
  Weiqin-Mo/Liquid-Glass-HTML (all MIT): rim light, sheen, and glass that
  needs detail behind it.
- Windows 98 control patterns from azayrahmad/win98-web (MIT),
  pollygon-dev/WIN98-template (Unlicense) and xero/windows98.website
  (CC0-1.0), written afresh in browser/ui/themes/win98.css.
- Gitguy268/QRcodeforeveryone (MIT, same author): sharing a page as a QR code.

ASSETS
------
branding/logo.svg, the icons generated from it and docs/img/*.png are this
project's own work, GPL-3.0 with the project. The pages use system fonts only.
Hillium Browser's wallpapers are drawn by code (browser/ui/shared/wallpaper.js;
the cloud sky comes from the author's MIT projects Qrer and Retrofind). No
Microsoft fonts, icons, sounds or wallpapers are included.

DEVELOPMENT TOOLS (not shipped)
-------------------------------
Playwright (Apache-2.0) drives Helium in tests/e2e.mjs and Hillium Browser in
browser/test/e2e.mjs. electron-builder (MIT) packages Hillium.app. uv (MIT/Apache-2.0)
creates SearXNG's Python environment. mkcert (BSD-3-Clause) and Docker run
the optional local services.
